.portability":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1913.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":188.5,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":52500.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1669.0,"requests":3}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the failed-classifier-JOB behavior explicitly: state whether a classifier that ERRORS routes to the full suite (which requires gating downstream `if:` on the job's *result*, not only its output, so full-route jobs run when the classifier concludes non-success) or hard-blocks Verified, and reconcile the Trust-contract 'selects full Verify' wording with the Routing 'blocks Verified' wording.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Trust contract: 'Failure to resolve the parent, an empty or malformed path list, classifier failure, or any non-allowlisted path selects full Verify.'","Routing: 'any classifier failure, missing lane, executed-job failure, or docs-gate failure blocks Verified.'","In GitHub Actions a downstream job that runs 'only on the full route' is gated by an `if:` reading the classifier job's OUTPUT; a job that FAILS produces no output, so both the full-route jobs and the docs-only job would evaluate their `if:` to false and skip (neither route executes) — the 'select full Verify' intent (run the full suite) and the 'block Verified' intent (hard -1) are different outcomes the plan does not reconcile.","Existing normalizer (scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py) fail-closes to 'failure' on skipped+failure_observed, which yields a -1 vote but NOT a full-suite run — so the two stated intents cannot both hold with the described output-gated mechanism."],"finding":"The route-selection mechanism does not specify how a FAILED classifier job (as opposed to a classifier that runs and returns a non-allowlisted verdict) actually causes the full lane to execute; the Trust contract says classifier failure 'selects full Verify' while Routing says it 'blocks Verified', and an output-gated full route cannot run when the job producing the output has itself failed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe35c78403d137c2f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Trust and diff contract ('classifier failure ... selects full Verify') vs Routing and aggregation ('any classifier failure ... blocks Verified'); Acceptance Criteria 'classifier failure ... selects full Verify' and 'A failed classifier or documentation gate cannot yield Verified +1'","norm_id":"n4cb41f04190a68cc","priority":0.75,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The trusted classifier step raises (git error, transient tooling failure) so the job concludes 'failure' rather than emitting a route verdict.","The classifier job times out or is cancelled mid-run."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Gate the full-route jobs on `always() && (needs.classifier.result != 'success' || needs.classifier.outputs.route == 'full')` so a classifier that fails/cancels still triggers the full suite, and gate the docs-only job on `needs.classifier.result == 'success' && needs.classifier.outputs.route == 'docs-only'`; keep the vote normalizer fail-closed so a classifier failure that somehow runs no lane still yields -1.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attribute